      "score": 33,
      "comments": 6,
      "author": "vinipsmaker",
      "published": "2026-09-20T14:13:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Linux sandboxing fundamentally relies on seccomp-bpf to filter system calls, combined with namespaces and cgroups for process resource isolation.",
        "Modern unprivileged sandboxing leverages the Landlock LSM for granular filesystem and network restrictions without requiring root privileges.",
        "Production boundaries increasingly adopt WebAssembly runtimes or microVMs like Firecracker and gVisor to prevent kernel exploit escapes."
      ]
